# ADR-0018 SpecTree specification-first ingestion

## Status
accepted

## Context
The application layer of the deterministic documentation pipeline is documented
after the fact: markdown pages, ADRs and policy IDs exist, but no machine-readable
specification tree links them to the compiled solution.
The Minotaur-Grammars repository defines eight line-based specification formats
(SrsSpec, AiSpec, TestSpec, ApiSpec, ModelSpec, NsSpec, AdrSpec, SolutionManifest)
for specification-first development.

## Decision
Adopt the SpecTree formats as first-class pipeline sources.
Specifications live in the same repository under example/spectree/, the grammar
files are vendored as pinned copies, and a deterministic Python 3 stdlib-only
parser (scripts/spectree-parse.py) emits versioned JSON ASTs under
docs/generated/spectree/ on every pipeline run.
The AST JSON schema (spectree/schemas/spectree-ast-v1.schema.json) is versioned
independently of the grammars so downstream gates can pin it.

## Consequences
- **Positive:** requirement, component and NFR data become queryable pipeline inputs
- **Positive:** the vendored grammars pin the exact syntax the parsers accept
- **Negative:** grammar changes in Minotaur-Grammars require a deliberate re-vendor bump
- **Neutral:** ASTs are git-ignored like all other generated artefacts

## Alternatives
- ANTLR-generated parsers from the grammar suite
- A .NET CLI tool distributed as a NuGet package

## Compliance
- component: spectree_parse must conform
- component: generate_docs must conform
